{
  "case_id": "2012-12-10",
  "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nSRI SRINIVASAN, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Petitioners.\nDAVID W. BOWKER, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Agency for International Development",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress's comprehensive program to address the worldwide problem of HIV and AIDS includes a policy of opposing prostitution and sex trafficking because they contribute to the diseases' spread. And correspondingly, Congress determined -- determined that the government should partner with and should grant limited competitive Federal funding to those organizations that agree with the policy opposing prostitution and sex trafficking because organizations that agree with that policy are most likely to carry out the Federal program in conformity with the Federal policy priorities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, but I guess the problem is that there are a number of different ways you could carry out the program. And let's say you have an organization that focuses on a particular -- you know, the administration of hospitals or whatever it is that's covered by the program, and they regard this issue as collateral to what they're concerned with. There -- there have to be some limitations on what type of loyalty oath you can require them to sign, isn't there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's your closest case -- your best case for the fact that you should get extra deference because this is the foreign affairs field? I mean, I think of U.S. v. Curtis Wright. Anything more specific than that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't see why this is a -- you talk about banning their speech. The government is just picking out who is an appropriate partner to -- to assist in this project. It wants to go and find people who, like them, are opposed to prostitution, and all they want to do is make sure that you're opposed to prostitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I'm -- I'm not quite sure I -- I see the difference, that the -- a conscientious Congressperson cannot -- can, in your view, say, I'm going to prefer organization A over organization B because I like their policies better --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're not going to go out there and do things to promote the legalization of prostitution because that's going to undermine our message. Those are two different positions, so tell me where you draw the line."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But -- but I guess what I'm -- I keep going back -- you keep going back and forth on this it -- it's not okay to tell me to take an oath of loyalty. But would it be okay for you to step outside the doors of this program and pass out literature that promotes the legalization of prostitution? Am I making my question clear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BOWKER",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think you can, in terms of viewpoint, either, Justice Breyer. I do think that the key -- the key that this Court outlined in Rust is the government's authority to control its program. And, if there is a threat to its program and the government needs to take some action in order to protect its program, prevent the message from being garbled or distorted, whatever the language is, then the government's case is strongest. Here, that is not at all what is happening."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose the government's interested in preventing and stopping the spread of malaria. And there's an organization that's marvelous at delivering the proper message for this, but they criticize the United States often. So they choose an organization that's not quite as good, but is quiet on these other issues. Is that permissible for the Congress to do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SRINIVASAN",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is not a matter of imposing a viewpoint on somebody. It's a matter of picking organizations with which to work who self-identify as having views that are commensurate with the government's views, so that they will be reliable in carrying out the government's program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0003-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One can understand why Congress would have wanted to tread with sensitivity when -- when we are dealing with foreign countries, especially foreign countries that have different views about prostitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-12-10",
      "confidence": 0.0,
